## 2. Folder Structure

We will use a modular structure. Here is the recommended setup (assuming a typical monorepo or two separate repositories):

```text
/college-app-root
│
├── /frontend               # Frontend Application (React/Vite)
│   ├── /public             # Static assets (images, icons)
│   ├── /src
│   │   ├── /assets         # Internal assets (fonts, SVGs)
│   │   ├── /components     # Reusable UI components (Buttons, Cards, Inputs)
│   │   ├── /features       # Domain-specific modules (auth, tasks, workouts, social)
│   │   ├── /hooks          # Custom React hooks
│   │   ├── /layouts        # Page layouts (Navbar, Sidebar, Footer)
│   │   ├── /pages          # Application pages (Home, Dashboard, Network)
│   │   ├── /services       # API client functions (Axios/Fetch)
│   │   ├── /store          # Global state management
│   │   ├── /utils          # Helper functions and constants
│   │   ├── App.jsx         # Root component
│   │   └── main.jsx        # Entry point
│   ├── package.json
│   └── tailwind.config.js
│
├── /backend                # Backend Server (Node/Express)
│   ├── /prisma             # Database schema and migrations
│   ├── /src
│   │   ├── /config         # Environment and DB config
│   │   ├── /controllers    # Request handlers (logic for endpoints)
│   │   ├── /middlewares    # Auth guards, error handlers, validation
│   │   ├── /models         # Data models / interfaces
│   │   ├── /routes         # Route definitions mapped to controllers
│   │   ├── /services       # Business logic operations (DB calls)
│   │   ├── /utils          # Helper functions (JWT generation, hashing)
│   │   └── server.js       # Express app initialization
│   ├── package.json
│   └── .env
```

